ABOUT THE ROLE:
This role is a permanent full-time position.
As a Principal Employee Relations, you will be responsible to provide support to the HR Leadership Team to develop and execute short / medium / long term ER strategies consistent with current and future trends in ER / IR practice. The Principal Employee Relations develops and maintains appropriate governance structures to ensure compliance with workplace relations legislation and global consistency.
Other key responsibilities include, but aren’t limited to:
Support HR Operations Managers in Africa to review and execute IR/ER documents;
Assist in delivery of Employee Relations activities for South32 functions in JHB;
Represent South32 in internal and external engagements, high-risk disputes and arbitrations as required (including CCMA referral matters for complex cases (HMM/Hillside) and full coverage for JHB Office. This may include initiating internal disciplinary proceedings;
Where required, act as an independent Chairperson to any internal South African cases deemed as dismissible offences or sensitive cases, for e.g. Harassment;
Provide ER legal advice in general to the South Africa Operations, as and when required;
Develop training content, as required for HR to deploy to line leaders;
Contribute to the development of ER procedures, guidelines and reporting requirements;
