About the job
We're on the lookout for a seasoned Senior Manager to take the lead in our Valuations team! If you're passionate about corporate actions, instrument pricing, and fund pricing across diverse portfolios—think life portfolios, collective investment schemes, and exchange-traded funds—this could be your perfect fit.
In this role, you'll be the mastermind behind valuation policies, procedures, and controls while leading a talented team. You'll also be the go-to expert for tackling complex valuation challenges and collaborating with key teams like Investment, Risk, and Compliance to keep everything running smoothly and in line with regulations. Plus, you’ll have the chance to drive process improvements, build strong stakeholder relationships, and stay ahead of industry trends and best practices.
Key responsibilities include:
Strategic leadership:
Managing the Valuations Committee and overseeing the Valuations Policy;
Provide strategic direction and leadership to the centralized Valuations team;
Collaborate with senior management to ensure valuation processes are aligned with regulatory requirements
Team Management:
Lead, manage, and develop a team of valuation professionals, providing guidance, coaching, and mentoring;
Ensure effective communication, coordination, and workflow management within the team;
Foster a culture of excellence, innovation, and continuous improvement.
Corporate Actions:
Oversee the processes and controls for processing and valuing corporate actions accurately and timeously, including mergers, acquisitions, spin-offs, capital repayments and dividend payments;
Assisting the team with the interpretation of complex corporate events;
Instrument Pricing:
Overseeing the processes and controls for the valuation of financial instruments including listed and unlisted equities (local and foreign), bonds, derivatives, pooled products, segregated portfolios, and alternative investments such as private equity and debt structures;
Ensure accurate and timely pricing, using market data, pricing models, and other relevant sources and ensuring instruments are priced according to the valuations policy;
Overseeing the design/automation of exception reporting.
Portfolio Pricing:
Overseeing the processes and controls for the valuation of life portfolios, pooled portfolios, segregated portfolios, collective investment schemes and exchange traded funds;
