About the job
Introduction
An exciting new opportunity has become available as a Senior Manager with Clientele. As the Senior Manager, you will be responsible for the development and implementation of lead generation strategies in line with the overall Clientele product and service offerings, developing the appropriate pipelines of leads from multiple channels, developing relationships with selected lead providers, developing media and digital strategies aligned to each channel, building proprietary intellectual capital around lead generation processes and systems, monitoring and reporting on channel and campaign effectiveness and value, collaborating closely with sales and marketing teams and contributing to the development and implementation of overall company marketing strategy.
Duties & Responsibilities
Strategy and Development
Drive the development and implementation of lead generation strategies for existing as well as new products and services;
Develop tailored media and digital strategies aligned to each channel and customer segment;
Develop and manage campaigns to attract leads, optimising value and effectiveness from each campaign through rigorous analytics and feedback;
Collaborate closely with Clientele's brand and digital experts to develop targeted, effective marketing messaging and media strategies;
Develop and imbed proprietary knowledge, systems and processes in connection with lead generation activities;
Contribute meaningfully to the continuous development, refinement and evaluation of the overall marketing strategy.
Systems and Analytics
Enhance systems and reports to measure and manage the effectiveness of lead-generation campaigns and channels;
Plan and deliver the appropriate lead volumes and types to meet hourly, daily, weekly, monthly and annual targets;
Continuously refine the measurement systems and processes based on research, feedback and best practice;
Contribute to the development of deep customer insights through competitor analysis;
Use analytics and customer insights to understand the performance of marketing strategies and use data and analytics to inform decisions around the marketing budgets.
Commercial and Expenditure Management
Manage the marketing budget and spending to optimise profitability and effectiveness of spend;
Negotiate prices/deals with all lead suppliers – including media owners and affiliates;
Reconcile supplier invoices and accounts;
Present Media plans and spending to the Group Executive team.
Continuous improvement
Make continuous trade-offs between volume and price of lead sources to optimise profitability, while continuously monitoring the financial effectiveness of all lead generation campaigns from inception rates/yield through to lapse rates;
Continuously monitor competitor activities and marketing spending and adjust marketing strategies accordingly.
Compliance and regulation
Display a thorough understanding and overview of the compliance and regulation environment as these relate to marketing and customer privacy;
Collaborate with relevant third parties to ensure all marketing activities meet all relevant compliance and regulatory requirements.
Communication and Collaboration
Work together with the Clientele Sales and Marketing/Brand team in terms of keeping up to date with operational changes and understand the impact of any changes on the products;
Work together with marketing to ensure that the product marketing is in line with the product benefits and where necessary, tweak the products;
Maintain and develop relationships with strategic lead provision partners and channels.
Leadership and management
Develop a team in support of lead generation strategies and activities;
Guide and mentor team members to achieve high performance and to grow skills and expertise in the team;
Collaborate across organisational boundaries as a member of senior management, advancing the achievement of overall goals and strategic initiatives.
Desired Experience & Qualification
Appropriate marketing and/or business tertiary qualification;
At least 10 years experience in direct marketing and campaign management of which at least 2 must have been at the senior management level.
Behavioural Competencies
Structured thinker with close attention to detail;
Strong numeric and analytical skills;
Strong written and interpersonal communication skills;
Proactive and self-driven;
A commercial and entrepreneurial bias;
Knowledge of the Financial Services Industry;
Operational experience in developing, implementing and managing tailored direct marketing campaigns and strategies;
Senior management experience in managing a team.

Purpose of the Job:
To assist the department in ensuring that the approved authorised Financial Services Providers (FSPs) and their Compliance Officers complies with the Financial Advisory and Intermediary Services (FAIS) legislation. The person appointed to these positions will report to the Manager.
Key Performance Areas:
Analyse annual financial statements and other statutory returns of Financial Services Providers to ensure that proper reporting standards have been followed;
Liaise with Financial Services Providers on issues of non-compliance identified during analysis of statutory returns;
Identify and report trends in the financial services sector with possible impact on the FSCA’s regulatory objectives;
Assess financial statements in line with the business model of Financial Services Providers;
Identify financial risks based on analysis of financial statements and any other financial information;
Analyse problems identified by regulated entities or as a result of new innovations and recommend solutions;
Support team members with analysis of other forms of financial reports;
Perform on-site inspection in terms of risk based supervision approach;
Liaison with various stakeholders; and
Assist the team with ad-hoc projects.
Other Key Competencies:
The candidate must demonstrate the following skills and attributes: A high level of judgement and a confident and decisive approach; problem analysis; attention to detail; information gathering; communication skills; good interpersonal skills and emotional intelligence; customer relations and persuasiveness skills.
FSCA is committed towards increasing the representation of marginalised groups in line with its Employment Equity Plan. Persons with disabilities are encouraged to apply.
Requirements
A Bachelor’s degree in commerce, law or related field with at least 3 to 4 years relevant experience of financial services industry or compliance management. The candidate must have good knowledge of Financial Advisory and Intermediary Act (FAIS Act), the Financial Sector Regulation Act, 9 of 2017 (FSR Act) and other relevant financial sector laws
