Job Description
THE JOB AT A GLANCE:
To plan, organize and control the activities in the Intake department, site pest control & bran and chop scheduling and schedule management
Responsibilities
WHAT YOU WILL DO:
Manage weighbridge and scale calibrations aligned to the National Regulator for Compulsory specifications (NRCS) and Trade Metrology Act;
Manage equipment services, calibration certificates and breakdown history;
Preventative maintenance in place and in line with DMS schedules;
Budgeting, motivation and implementation of Capital Expenditure and Major Repairs & Maintenance projects;
Develop and manage departmental Five Year Facility Plan;
Manages grain receipt and stock movement;
Co-ordinates and manages daily, weekly and monthly stock counts;
Declares and reconciles wheat & maize stocks;
Identifies, investigates and resolves stock variances;
Compiles and manages grain orders and off-loading to ensure no demurrage changes are incurred;
Initiate and report on Continuous Improvement projects;
Maintain consumable stock levels (fumigants & pesticides);
Prepare and manage annual production budget from zero base;
Ensure compliance to quality specifications and Grading Regulations;
Maintain FSSC 22000 & ISO 14001 programs;
Maintain Good Manufacturing Practices;
Maintain the Grain Receipt and Stock Management Procedure;
Co-ordinate staff training needs and keep a register / evidence of training conducted;
Establish and agree IPA’s. Review and keep record of performance on a quarterly basis;
Ensure company policies, procedures and job profiles are available and adhered to;
Implement and maintain good housekeeping and sanitation standards;
Maintain fumigation treatments in accordance with schedules;
Ensure duties are carried out in accordance with the PCO letter of appointment;
Conduct monthly Pest control audits and follow-up on non-conformances raised;
Co-ordinate and trend insect sighting’s, prioritize and implement corrective actions for the purpose of continuous improvement;
Attend fumigation refresher training and maintain PCO registration with the DoA;
Implement, maintain and review the Railway Regulatory system;
Train staff and ensure compliance to the Railway Safety Regulations;
Maintain the wheat grouping and binning procedures to ensure optimal grist consistency;
Assure that labour relations are handled according to company policy and legislation in your department to assure sound labour relations;
Responsible for health-, hygiene- and safety standards in this department within laid down policies and relevant legislation;
Liaise with Procurement department on raw materials (wheat & maize) on quantities and qualities required for milling;
Liaise with Spoornet and delivery contractors to assure that raw materials arrive on planned dates;
Scheduling and schedule management and customer liaison of bran and chop sales.
Qualifications
ESSENTIAL SKILLS & QUALIFICATIONS:
Core knowledge – Diploma/degree in agricultural business, with Grade 12 Mathematics & Science. Qualified wheat and maize grader. Certificate in grains bag, bulk, circulation & structural fumigation and registered as a PCO with DoA.
Excellent computer literacy essential: Excel and Oracle.
Academic – Analytical skill, Problem solving, Creative and solution orientated , Self-motivated, capable of working independently and delivering on time, An assertive, goal oriented self-starter with good interpersonal and organizing skills, Detail orientated and decision-making skills
Leadership – Owning it!, Driving long-term results, Staying a step-ahead
Personal Effectiveness – Effective communication, Interpersonal skills, Integrity, Creativity, Continuous learning
Experience
