CONVEYANCING ATTORNEY IN CAPE TOWN
Our client is looking for a dynamic Conveyancing attorney to run their property division in Cape Town.
The position will entail both attending to and supervising conveyancing transactions.
Duties and Responsibilities
Receiving and perusing instructions to attend to conveyancing and associated matters;
Drafting various conveyancing documents accurately and independently;
Liaising with clients, city councils, SARS, managing agents, banks and linked attorney firms;
Preparing and checking documents for lodgement, ensuring all conditions are met and processes followed in order for transactions to be registered successfully at the relevant Deeds Registry;
Attending to and checking all financial aspects of transactions, including pro-forma and final reconciliation statements of account;
Provision of legal advisory services;
Assisting with the effective and efficient management of all conveyancing and related matters;
Assisting with the operational requisites of the conveyancing department; and
Assisting with marketing, managing existing relationships and new business development.
Skills and knowledge
In depth knowledge and understanding of conveyancing and related areas of law;
Meticulous attention to detail;
Excellent command of the English language;
Excellent communication and written skills and ability to liaise with clients, banks and colleagues in a professional and effective manner;
Ability to work independently and to effectively manage high volumes of work; and
Team player with good interpersonal skills, showing an eagerness to assist others within the department, as well as a willingness to learn.
Desired Experience & Qualification:
MUST have experience with conveyancing transactions in Cape Town
LLB law degree
Admitted conveyancer
Minimum of 5 years practice experience in Conveyancing
Admitted attorney
Admitted conveyancer
Admission as a Notary would be an advantage
Additional Requirements
Presentable and professional
Advanced computer literacy (Microsoft and legal software programs)
Contactable references
Critical Behavioural Competencies

