ABOUT THE ROLE:
This role is a permanent full-time position supporting our operations in the Northern Cape province, however reporting to our Johannesburg (Melrose Arch) functional hub offices. As a specialist transformation, you will be responsible for effectively supporting the management, monitoring, and tracking of all Transformation activities such as advising the element owners on various legislative changes, managing Risks related to HMM license to operate, forming part of different internal and external Transformation committees, plans and expenditure for HMM operations while ensuring that all related risks are adequately managed and mitigated.
Other key responsibilities include, but aren’t limited to:
Capture all administrative duties on legislative reporting on Mining charter reports, Annual SLP reports,
B-BBEE Commission reports assigned to them;
Review and consolidate all the B-BBEE reports shared by various element owners during the audit;
Consolidate all the Mining Charter reports shared by various element owners during the reporting cycle;
Review and Consolidate all the SLP implementation and annual reports shared by various element owners during the reporting cycle;
Consolidate all HMM B-BBEE Commission reports shared by various element owners including Hillside;
Onboard and Create purchase requisition for all new Transformation related service providers;
Effectively manage relationships with internal and external stakeholders;
Support by performing processing activities to ensure Service Level Agreements are met, as well as knowledge of processing is current;
Liaise internally with the Transformation and Diversity committee (Develop agendas, presentations, Capture minutes and share same).
ABOUT YOU:
You will have experience and demonstrate capability in the following:
Minimum 5 years relevant professional experience;
Specialised knowledge in Transformation, MPRDA, Mining Charter, and B-BBEE Act (Employment Equity, Enterprise Development and Supplier Development, Local Economic Development, Human Resource Development);
Experience in SAP would be preferred;
Experience with working in teams in a high-paced environment;
Knowledge of internal control environment and regulatory requirements.
Qualifications for this role are:
Grade 12 or Matric Certificate;
High Certificate, National Diploma or Bachelors in Human Resource Management, Training Management, Industrial Psychology, Labour Relations, Labour Relations Law or related qualification in business

Key Responsibilities:
Regulatory Compliance:
Ensure timely and accurate submission of regulatory reports, including Basel III capital adequacy reports, liquidity coverage ratio (LCR), and net stable funding ratio (NSFR);
Stay updated on local and international regulatory requirements (e.g., central banks, Basel Committee, IFRS).
Reporting:
Oversee the preparation of regulatory reports, including financial statements, capital adequacy, risk-weighted assets, and liquidity metrics;
Validate and reconcile data for accuracy and completeness before submission.
Stakeholder Management:
Liaise with regulatory authorities, internal and external auditors to address queries and provide necessary information;
Communicate regulatory changes and their impact to senior management and relevant stakeholders.
Data Management and Governance:
Implement robust data governance frameworks to ensure data integrity and consistency;
Oversee the extraction, validation, and transformation of data to meet reporting requirements.
Policy Implementation:
Develop and maintain policies and procedures for regulatory reporting to align with compliance standards and best practices;
Update internal processes and systems to adhere to changes in regulatory frameworks.
Risk and Issue Management:
Identify and mitigate risks associated with non-compliance or reporting errors;
Develop contingency plans to address gaps or delays in reporting processes.
System Enhancements:
Collaborate with IT and finance teams to enhance or implement reporting systems, including data automation and reporting tools;
Ensure reporting systems are adaptable to evolving regulatory changes.
Strategic Planning:
Provide insights and analysis on regulatory trends to inform senior management’s strategic decisions;
Monitor regulatory developments and assess their impact on the bank’s operations and capital structure.
Audit and Review:
Coordinate with internal and external auditors for reviews of regulatory reports and processes;
Maintain documentation and audit trails for all submitted reports.
Qualifications and Experience:
Qualified Chartered Accountant (CA(SA));
5+ years of experience in regulatory reporting within the banking or financial services industry;
In-depth knowledge of Basel III, IFRS, and local regulatory frameworks;
Strong leadership, communication, and stakeholder management skills;
Experience with data governance and reporting systems is highly advantageous.

